The test passes `grads = [None]` and one trainable variable into `optimizer.apply(...)`. In `BaseOptimizer.apply`, the gradients and variables are sent to `_filter_empty_gradients`. That helper removes every `None` gradient from `filtered_grads`; with this input, the list becomes empty. The next check is `if not filtered_grads: raise ValueError("No gradients provided for any variable.")`, so the exception type is `ValueError` and the message is exactly that string.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"No gradients provided for any variable.","exception_type":"ValueError"}
